1. \*At the time of enrollment, participants must be aged 60 or above, of either gender, and able to provide legal identification;
2. Have the ability to understand the clinical trial procedures, voluntarily agree to participate, and sign the informed consent form;
3. Be able to cooperate and participate in all scheduled follow-ups as required by the protocol;
4. Female trial participants should have undergone menopause or sterilization surgery; \[Menopause is defined as continuous cessation of menstruation for ≥12 months without alternative medical measures; sterilization surgery includes bilateral tubal ligation, bilateral oophorectomy, or hysterectomy\].
5. Trial participants who are judged by the researchers to have stable health conditions. \[Stable health conditions refer to those with chronic diseases that have been stable for the past 3 months prior to enrollment, such as diabetes, hypertension, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, and asthma. If the researchers judge the condition to be stable, the participant is allowed to participate in this trial\].

Exclusion Criteria:

(If the enrollment requirement is not met, and the criteria described in the "\*" option are met during screening, the visit can be rescheduled)

1. \*On the day before vaccination, the on-site measured temperature is \>37.0℃ (axillary temperature);
2. \*Upon research, the on-site measured blood oxygen saturation (SpO2) is ≤90%;
3. Have previously received or plan to receive any marketed or experimental RSV vaccine/RSV monoclonal antibody;
4. A history of RSV infection confirmed within 6 months prior to enrollment;
5. \*Having used or planning to use any non-specific immunoglobulin and/or blood products containing non-specific immunoglobulin (such as whole blood, plasma) within 3 months before enrollment or during the trial period;
6. \*Have used other investigational or unregistered products (drugs or vaccines) within one month before enrollment, or are currently participating in other clinical trials or plan to participate in other clinical trials during the trial period;
