8. \*Having received a live attenuated vaccine within 30 days before enrollment or planning to receive one within 30 days after enrollment, or having received any non-live vaccine other than the trial vaccine within 14 days before enrollment or planning to receive one within 14 days after enrollment;
9. \*Having an acute disease or being in an acute exacerbation phase of a chronic disease within 3 days before enrollment, or using antipyretic analgesics (excluding medications used to control current diseases and which, in the investigator's judgment, are not expected to affect the interpretation of trial results, such as aspirin used for the treatment of coronary heart disease) or antiallergic medications (e.g., acetaminophen, ibuprofen, aspirin, loratadine, cetirizine, etc.);
10. Individuals with a history of severe allergic reactions requiring medical intervention to any vaccine or medication \[such as anaphylactic shock, allergic laryngeal edema, allergic purpura, thrombocytopenic purpura, local allergic necrotic reaction (Arthus reaction), etc.\] or known allergies to any component of the trial vaccine \[citric acid, sodium citrate, sodium chloride, sucrose, polysorbate 80 (II), mannitol, squalene, sorbitan trioleate (Span 85), water for injection\];
11. Previous or current congenital or acquired immune deficiency diseases (such as AIDS), human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection, systemic lupus erythematosus, or other autoimmune diseases that may affect the trial evaluation as assessed by the investigator (such as a history of inflammatory demyelinating neuropathy like Guillain-Barré syndrome); other diseases affecting immune function (such as asplenia or functional asplenia);
